nmos-dcm (2.2.9+mxl1-5) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add DcMxlSender (nmosconnection/dcMxlSender.py): mxl senders now use
    it instead of the plain MxlSender, so GET .../active/ reflects a real
    disk check of the domain directory (mxl_enabled true/false based on
    whether <domain>/<flow_id>.mxl-flow/flow_def.json actually exists;
    available_flows lists what's really there when no flow_id is staged
    yet) instead of purely reflecting in-memory state. mxl-fabrics-proxy
    itself stays statically configured - not queried directly.
  * nmosDriver.py's addMxlSenderToIS05 now registers real local
    interfaces (getAvailableInterfaces()) instead of the demo-only
    generateRandomUnicast(), so source_ip's "auto" resolution reflects a
    real interface on this host.

